# User-Agent policy — Marble Descent

Marble Descent is a **neon plinko / marble-drop arcade**, NOT a
slot-machine theme. The User-Agent must therefore stay a plain,
realistic Android Chrome string — WITHOUT the `appid/… appname/…`
suffix that the account's slot-themed games (Zeus / Joker / Magma
/ Egypt) carry.

Rules:

- Format: `Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android <ver>; <brand> <model>
  Build/<tag>) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko)
  Chrome/149.0.7220.24 Mobile Safari/537.36`
- Chrome major version is bumped to **149** (encoded in
  `lib/glyph/glyph_pack.dart`).
- The version fragments are decoded through `glyph_codec` — never
  hard-coded at the call site.
- The device brand / model / build tag come from `device_info_plus`
  at first call to `UaStampClient.warmUp()`.
- Both the HTTP client (`marbleWire`) AND the WebView
  (`_web.setUserAgent(marbleWire.stamp)`) MUST use the same string.
- No `Dart/…`, `Flutter/…`, `WebView` / `wv/`, or package-name
  tokens anywhere in the UA.

If a future project on this account turns Marble Descent into a
slot theme (unlikely), consult
`.cursor/rules/marble_gray_guide.md` and the account-wide
`gray_user_agent.mdc` before adding an `appid` / `appname` suffix.
